{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}+8x+50y=129?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-10418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}+8x+50y & =129 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x-5{y}^{2}+50y & =129 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x-5[{y}^{2}-10y] & =129 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-16-5[(y-5)^{2}-25] & =129 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-16-5(y-5)^{2}+125 & =129 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-5(y-5)^{2} & =129+16-125 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-5(y-5)^{2} & =20 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{20}-\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(-4,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-10418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7b1d37f15cdb5956954e977b7c08ecd903bdab53ccb8afdec35f2e82262c8fc"} {"question" "q-10418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-10418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,5)"] ["math" "(-4,5)"] ["math" "(2,-5)"] ["math" "(5,-2)"] ["math" "(5,-4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-10418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-4,5)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-78868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{9}-(x+4)^{2}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-78868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{1}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-4$ and $k=7.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-4,7).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-78868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7b1d37f15cdb5956954e977b7c08ecd903bdab53ccb8afdec35f2e82262c8fc"} {"question" "q-78868" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-78868" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,9)"] ["math" "(-4,7)"] ["math" "(4,-7)"] ["math" "(7,-4)"] ["math" "(9,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-78868" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-4,7)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-116113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$4{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}-40x+6y=-85?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-116113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}-40x+6y & =-85 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-40x-3{y}^{2}+6y & =-85 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}-10x]-3[{y}^{2}-2y] & =-85 \\\\ 4[(x-5)^{2}-25]-3[(y-1)^{2}-1] & =-85 \\\\ 4(x-5)^{2}-100-3(y-1)^{2}+3 & =-85 \\\\ 4(x-5)^{2}-3(y-1)^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(5,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-116113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7b1d37f15cdb5956954e977b7c08ecd903bdab53ccb8afdec35f2e82262c8fc"} {"question" "q-116113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-116113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-5,-1)"] ["math" "(1,5)"] ["math" "(3,4)"] ["math" "(4,-3)"] ["math" "(5,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-116113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(5,1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-274640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-36y+8x=4$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-274640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-36y+8x & =4 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-36y-4{x}^{2}+8x & =4 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}-4y]-4[{x}^{2}-2x] & =4 \\\\ 9[(y-2)^{2}-4]-4[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =4 \\\\ 9(y-2)^{2}-36-4(x-1)^{2}+4 & =4 \\\\ 9(y-2)^{2}-4(x-1)^{2} & =4+36-4 \\\\ 9(y-2)^{2}-4(x-1)^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,2\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-274640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7b1d37f15cdb5956954e977b7c08ecd903bdab53ccb8afdec35f2e82262c8fc"} {"question" "q-274640" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-274640" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-274640" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-274640" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-328394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+36y+10x=25$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-328394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+36y+10x & =25 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+36y-{x}^{2}+10x & =25 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}+4y]-[{x}^{2}-10x] & =25 \\\\ 9[(y+2)^{2}-4]-[(x-5)^{2}-25] & =25 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-36-(x-5)^{2}+25 & =25 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-(x-5)^{2} & =25+36-25 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-(x-5)^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{36} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(\\,5,-2\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-328394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7b1d37f15cdb5956954e977b7c08ecd903bdab53ccb8afdec35f2e82262c8fc"} {"question" "q-328394" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-328394" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-328394" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"} {"question" "q-328394" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030712/state.json" "file_sha256" "f2ea3a8af2da59abfb48f7a575f58eb4075750a1563c382b374d6ee53a87f3cf"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1205 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
